1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,378
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:07,424
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,635
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,893
[Martina] <i>Your own man eluded you?</i>

7
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:20,687
What if he reports to the police?

8
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:22,105
[Red] <i>I'm not worried about the police.</i>

9
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:24,190
<i>I'm worried he might tell Atoy.</i>

10
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:25,191
[thuds]

11
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:27,235
[Atoy] <i>Do you know where</i>
<i>your father will be tomorrow?</i>

12
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:30,030
I just need to ask him something.

13
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:32,866
- [thumping]
- [grunting and groaning]

14
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,409
[Martina] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

15
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:35,994
<i>Audrey isn't here, and Janine--</i>

16
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:37,662
Don't meddle here. Move!

17
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:40,123
[Emerson] <i>He knows who killed his father.</i>

18
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:42,375
- Your brother, Red.
- [Audrey gasps]

19
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:43,460
PREVIOUSLY

20
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:44,919
- [Dmitri, in English] <i>What's happening?</i>
- [Martina, in English] <i>Dad.</i>

21
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,171
[Dmitri] <i>Is there a shootout?</i>

22
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,631
[Martina, in English] <i>We have a problem.</i>
<i>Atoy is here. I think he's after Red.</i>

23
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:52,761
- [grunting and groaning]
- [thumping]

24
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:53,678
[gunfire]

25
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:55,138
[staff on phone] <i>They're shooting</i>
<i>at each other</i>

26
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,807
<i>- at the firing range.</i>
- [Audrey] <i>Dad, stop Atoy!</i>

27
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:00,560
- [growls]
- [thumps]

28
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:02,812
You animal. Now I know the truth.

29
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,315
[Atoy] <i>You killed my father!</i>

30
00:01:05,398 --> 00:01:07,942
[Dmitri] <i>You won't get your father back</i>
<i>if you kill Red.</i>

31
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:10,236
He didn't just take a life,

32
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,196
he took away time.

33
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:12,822
<i>Time I could have spent with my father.</i>

34
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:14,449
<i>So, I will also kill your son.</i>

35
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:23,208
[music concludes]

36
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:26,044
[Audrey gasping]

37
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:29,672
[pensive music playing]

38
00:01:29,756 --> 00:01:30,882
[car door slams shut]

39
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:32,008
[suspicious music playing]

40
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:33,259
[in English] My God.

41
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:35,428
[gasps]

42
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:36,471
Atoy.

43
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:38,807
Atoy.

44
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:44,145
[music fades]

45
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:49,943
[monotonous melancholic music playing]

46
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:57,826
[somber music playing]

47
00:01:57,909 --> 00:02:00,537
[melodramatic music playing]

48
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:06,084
- [in English] Dad! Dad! Dad, Dad!
- [in English] Oh my God. Oh my God!

49
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:08,920
- [in English] Oh my God!
- [in English] Dad! Dad, Dad, Dad.

50
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:10,964
[Martina, in English] Oh my God! [sobs]

51
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:13,967
[Audrey screams] Dad!

52
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:19,597
[in English] Oh my God! Oh my God!

53
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:21,558
[in English] Oh my God!

54
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:23,309
[Martina sobs, in English] Oh my God.

55
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:27,272
- [in English] Dad! Dad.
- [in English] Oh my God!

56
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:29,023
[in English] Dad!

57
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:39,159
[music fades]

58
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:44,330
[dramatic music playing]

59
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:46,833
Call an ambulance!

60
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:49,127
- [sobbing]
- [in English] Dad!

61
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,587
[in English] You shot him!

62
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:52,338
- He didn't do anything to you!
- [in English] Dad!

63
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:56,968
[music swells]

64
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:00,972
[in English] Dad, Dad!

65
00:03:01,055 --> 00:03:06,311
[sobbing]

66
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,688
[in English] Dad!

67
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:10,690
[echoing]

68
00:03:10,773 --> 00:03:15,904
[suave theme music playing]

69
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:17,322
[motorcycle revving]

70
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:19,240
[sewing machine whirring]

71
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,784
- [scratches]
- [snipping]

72
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:25,121
[sewing machine clacking]

73
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:28,499
- [gun cocks]
- [multiple gunfire]

74
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:31,502
[clacking]

75
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:32,879
[snipping]

76
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:34,923
[music swells]

77
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:41,763
Wait! Who are you?!

78
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:43,431
That woman started it!

79
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:47,310
You know, I could have you all jailed
for assault!

80
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,895
Cathy, you started it!

81
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,023
You said it yourself. Get ready, Karla!

82
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:54,943
Hey, hey, hey! I recorded you.

83
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:57,195
The video clearly shows you started it,

84
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,864
and you came here to hurt Karla!

85
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,574
- I'll upload this.
- Upload it.

86
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:02,909
- Go ahead, upload it.
- [overlapping chatter]

87
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:04,410
- No, no! Please, please!
- [Jona] So she learns her lesson!

88
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:05,578
No, don't, please!

89
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,663
[in English] Request denied.

90
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,498
- You'll be canceled now.
- Hmm, canceled.

91
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:09,958
Don't.

92
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:12,752
Be thankful Karla is kind.

93
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:17,131
So, leave Karla alone, you leeches!

94
00:04:17,215 --> 00:04:18,800
- [neighbors] Leave!
- [scoffs]

95
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:19,884
- [woman] Leave!
- [indistinct]

96
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,886
- Get out of here!
- [Jona] Leave!

97
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:22,845
- [Jona] Why are you staring?!
- [indistinct]

98
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:25,098
- Get out of here now! Leave!
- [Cathy scoffs]

99
00:04:25,181 --> 00:04:27,100
- Bye! Leave!
- [car door clicks shut]

100
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:28,434
[Mona] Don't come back here.

101
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,061
- [Jona, in English] True!
- [Mona] Leave!

102
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:31,813
- [woman] Bye!
- [T-Bak] Don't come back, okay!

103
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:32,897
[Mona] Don't ever come back here.

104
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,399
[T-Bak] You're enemies!

105
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:36,609
[indistinct]

106
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:38,861
Ah, Karla, don't cry.

107
00:04:40,196 --> 00:04:41,656
[Karla] I don't want trouble anymore.

108
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:44,033
I don't want more problems.

109
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:48,454
Karla, we're here if you have problems.

110
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:49,789
[T-Bak] Yes.

111
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:52,125
We won't leave you.

112
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:53,167
[sentimental music playing]

113
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:55,169
We'll be with you! Right?

114
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:56,796
- [all] That's right!
- [Jona] Yes, we're here.

115
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:58,256
[T-Bak] Don't cry.

116
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:09,517
[music fades]

117
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:14,397
[Martina] Where's your Atoy?

118
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,774
Where's the man you always defend?

119
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:20,945
Oh? Why can't you look at me?

120
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:22,572
[in English] You know,
this is all Atoy's fault,

121
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:23,948
but this is also on you!

122
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:25,825
It was wrong to get back
together in the first place,

123
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:28,077
then you brought him into our family?!

124
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:30,413
Why are you blaming me?!

125
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:34,042
This wouldn't have happened if Red
hadn't done something to Atoy's father!

126
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:36,210
He didn't mean it, Audrey.

127
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:40,298
Martina, you and I both know
your husband is a bad man.

128
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:42,925
"Didn't mean it" doesn't exist for him.

129
00:05:43,009 --> 00:05:44,427
He ran away from the crime.

130
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:47,597
[in English] Now, he has to face
the consequences and deal with it!

131
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,932
- [huffs]
- [tense music playing]

132
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,602
[in English] I know you hate your brother.

133
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:55,271
But to involve Dad in his anger?

134
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:56,856
[in English] That is monstrous!

135
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:59,609
He didn't mean it.

136
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:01,069
I know Atoy.

137
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:02,361
[music fades]

138
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:03,738
[Martina] Are you blind?!

139
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:05,531
[in English] Or just plain stupid?

140
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:06,866
[in English] You were there!

141
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:09,869
[in English] You saw him
shoot your own father!

142
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:11,370
Your brother was beaten to a pulp!

143
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:13,164
My husband!

144
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:15,208
Don't defend him, Audrey!

145
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:18,377
For once, side with your own family!

146
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,546
[tense music playing]

147
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:21,631
[Martina sighs sharply]

148
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:29,722
His phone is still off.

149
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,224
[clicks tongue]

150
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:32,809
[sighs]

151
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:36,521
What time is Mommy coming back?

152
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:39,649
And why isn't Daddy here yet?

153
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:41,984
They're probably on their way back.

154
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:45,947
[wind chimes clinking]

155
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,326
[sneaky music playing]

156
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:51,953
It's just you.

157
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:54,747
[smirks] Why do you even

158
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,415
come here?

159
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,376
You don't live here.

160
00:06:58,459 --> 00:06:59,794
I'm not forbidden here, am I?

161
00:07:02,171 --> 00:07:03,756
- [music ends]
- [wind chimes clinking]

162
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,674
- [Cita] Atoy.
- [Ibyang] Tatoy?

163
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:05,758
Daddy?

164
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,927
[Cita] What happened?

165
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:12,557
[suspicious music playing]

166
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,853
Daddy, I thought you were with Mommy?

167
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:19,313
She said

168
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:21,858
she was going to see you.

169
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:24,527
Daddy?

170
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:32,201
Tatoy, what happened to your hand?

171
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,119
Is that blood?

172
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:34,829
It's nothing.

173
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,876
[tense music playing]

174
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:57,059
[music fades]

175
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:58,478
[sighs]

176
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:04,567
[somber music playing]

177
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:05,902
[sobs]

178
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:08,070
- [in English] Hey.
- [in English] Dad.

179
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:10,573
[Audrey, in English] How are you feeling?

180
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,826
[in English] I'm okay.

181
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:17,747
- [smirks] At least, still alive.
- [Audrey sighs]

182
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:25,213
Red? Where is he?

183
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:26,672
How is he?

184
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:28,382
He's fine, Dad.

185
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:31,469
He's in another room with Martina.

186
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:40,228
[in English] Dad. Dad…

187
00:08:42,813 --> 00:08:44,899
What really happened?

188
00:08:47,985 --> 00:08:50,404
[in English] I saw him fire his gun, but…

189
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,907
I'm not sure.

190
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:58,287
Did Atoy really mean to shoot you?

191
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:02,792
[gunshot]

192
00:09:05,169 --> 00:09:06,587
[in English] Yes, he did.

193
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:08,798
[Audrey gasps]

194
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:11,592
Red couldn't fight against Atoy anymore,

195
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,970
so I stepped in.

196
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:19,725
I asked him to stop, but he still shot me.

197
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:25,231
He lost his father, so he targeted me.

198
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:28,693
He's not that kind of person, Dad.

199
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:31,571
Atoy is reasonable.

200
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,365
There's no rhyme or reason for someone

201
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:38,119
who's full of anger and revenge.

202
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,204
[sighs]

203
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,372
My child…

204
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,667
[in English] I want to see you happy.

205
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:49,088
But what will happen
to your relationship now?

206
00:09:49,171 --> 00:09:51,257
[somber music playing]

207
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,301
[in English] How can you be with him?

208
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:55,553
[melancholic music playing]

209
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:57,471
He's furious with your family,

210
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:00,850
to the point he dragged me into it.

211
00:10:05,229 --> 00:10:07,440
I want to press charges against him.

212
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:12,278
But I'm thinking of you and Janine.

213
00:10:12,361 --> 00:10:14,739
Don't, Dad. Please.

214
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:16,490
Don't go through with it.

215
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:21,245
He's still Janine's father, and I know…

216
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:24,540
[in English] I know
he's a good person deep inside.

217
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,125
Is it that easy?

218
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,587
[in English] Just let him go
after what he did,

219
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,547
and just go back to normal?

220
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,049
[music fades]

221
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:35,968
The situation is too complicated.

222
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:38,846
[in English] I just hope

223
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:43,100
you make the right decision
for you and Janine.

224
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:48,397
[epic music playing]

225
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:57,657
Babe, are you sure Karla did that to you?

226
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,618
I just wanted to talk to her
about last night,

227
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:03,287
but she took it the wrong way!

228
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,539
She and her friends ganged up on me!

229
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:06,999
- [clicks tongue]
- [pensive music playing]

230
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,045
[in English] Karla can be
a bit rough sometimes,

231
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:13,005
but it-- it's for a good reason.

232
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:15,800
- I'll talk to her.
- [Cathy, in English] No!

233
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:18,010
She'll just twist it.

234
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:20,304
She'll say I started it,

235
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,181
but that's not true!

236
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:23,974
That's not true, Gavin!

237
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:26,560
That it's all my fault. That's not true!

238
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:31,399
- [phone vibrating]
- [sinister music playing]

239
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:33,567
[in English] I'll just take this call.

240
00:11:34,985 --> 00:11:36,654
Mom, I'll be home in a while.

241
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:39,698
Why are you at the hospital?

242
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:40,699
[music fades]

243
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,284
- Hey, Karla!
- Oh?

244
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,202
[chuckles]

245
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:44,370
How are you?

246
00:11:44,453 --> 00:11:45,788
- Hey.
- You, how are you?

247
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:49,041
Karla, any news about Atoy?

248
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:50,459
I don't know.

249
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:53,045
I haven't been to the shop.
I'm upset with him.

250
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:57,091
He even forbade Gavin
from being friends with me.

251
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:58,259
What's his deal?

252
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:00,636
[somber music playing]

253
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:02,388
Gavin…

254
00:12:03,347 --> 00:12:05,057
Gavin Regalia, Red's son?

255
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,643
Yes. Why, brother?

256
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:10,646
Your Brother Atoy did the right thing.

257
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:12,606
Stay away from that guy for now.

258
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:15,651
Because his father has a bad reputation?

259
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,486
But Gavin is different from him.

260
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:21,157
Karla, Gavin's father was the one
who hit-and-run Sir Delfin.

261
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,450
[heavy music playing]

262
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:23,659
What?

263
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:27,496
Are you sure?

264
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:30,708
Yes.

265
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:34,712
Atoy already confronted Red. They fought.

266
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:39,675
So, for your safety, please,

267
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:41,343
stay away from Gavin.

268
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:44,805
[music fades]

269
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:47,016
So, what's your plan now?

270
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:50,686
What if Red retaliates
because of what you did?

271
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:53,981
You shouldn't have let your temper
get the better of you!

272
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:56,275
I don't know.

273
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:57,985
- [inhales]
- [pensive music playing]

274
00:12:58,068 --> 00:13:01,113
I'm only thinking of Audrey and Janine.

275
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,199
Talk to Audrey.

276
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:04,658
The three of you should move away.

277
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:07,119
Start as a family.

278
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:10,331
[knocking on door]

279
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:14,668
[door lock rattling]

280
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:17,004
[wind chimes clinking]

281
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,341
[music fades]

282
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:24,845
See, I told you. Talk to her.

283
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:29,016
[pensive music playing]

284
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:31,268
- Audrey.
- [Audrey] Let's talk later.

285
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:33,395
- Audrey.
- Atoy, I'll just get Janine.

286
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:35,272
Audrey. Audrey, let's talk for a moment.

287
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:37,233
- I came from the hospital. I'm tired.
- Audrey.

288
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:40,194
I understand your hatred for Red.

289
00:13:41,278 --> 00:13:43,364
But why did you involve Dad?

290
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:48,202
He had nothing to do with you.

291
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:51,664
Why?

292
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:56,210
Audrey.

293
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,674
- I didn't mean to hurt your father.
- You did!

294
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:04,093
- [Atoy] No!
- You shot him!

295
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:05,553
- I didn't shoot him!
- He's in the hospital now

296
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:06,637
because of you!

297
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,597
Audrey, listen to me!

298
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:10,474
I was shooting Red!

299
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:14,937
He used your father as a shield.

300
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:18,440
I had no intention
of involving your father. Believe me.

301
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:20,150
Who told you that?

302
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:21,569
Red?

303
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:23,571
- Martina?
- Dad.

304
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,824
He himself told me.

305
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:30,244
[music fades]

306
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:33,205
[scoffs] But your father hates me, right?

307
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:35,666
He doesn't want me for you, right?

308
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:37,042
Maybe he's lying to you.

309
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,837
- No…
- It's not just Dad who's lying here.

310
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:42,840
You planned your attack.

311
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:45,092
Didn't you? That's why you texted me,

312
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:48,178
so we wouldn't see what you'd do
to my brother and dad, huh?!

313
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:49,763
[pensive music playing]

314
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,473
Because I didn't want you involved.

315
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,767
But why didn't you tell me?!

316
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:58,022
Why did I have to learn
from Emerson what Red did, huh?!

317
00:14:59,064 --> 00:15:00,149
[in English] We had a good thing!

318
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:03,277
[in English] I trusted you!

319
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:06,655
Why did you do that. Why?!

320
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,490
You shouldn't have attacked!

321
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:10,868
Hey. Audrey!

322
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:11,994
[gasps]

323
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:16,373
You're not in a position to tell me that.

324
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,584
[in English] Eight years.

325
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:23,172
Eight years I carried the weight
of losing my father, Audrey.

326
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:26,216
For eight years, the man
who killed my father walked free,

327
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,135
and it's none other than your brother!

328
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:31,847
And then he has the audacity to face me
like nothing happened.

329
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:36,018
So, you have no right to tell me
what I should or shouldn't do!

330
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:40,689
[epic music playing]

331
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:43,651
- Please understand me, Audrey.
- [sobs]

332
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,528
I'm furious with Red.

333
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:51,241
But I had no intention
of involving your father.

334
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:52,785
None.

335
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:54,912
‪[Audrey sobs]

336
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:57,373
Okay.

337
00:15:58,415 --> 00:16:01,293
Let's say you're telling the truth.

338
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:06,507
You hurt Red, which he deserves.

339
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:10,094
But what if he retaliates?

340
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:13,722
[melancholic music playing]

341
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:15,265
I'm not afraid of him.

342
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:18,227
But your conflict won't end!

343
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:21,188
And I can't stop you both.

344
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:26,694
[in English] You almost killed my father!

345
00:16:29,279 --> 00:16:30,614
Whether you meant it or not,

346
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,158
will we still be okay after this?

347
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:36,704
[in English] Things will never
be the same, Atoy.

348
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:41,000
Audrey, we can start again. Right?

349
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:43,877
Then let's move away, the three of us.

350
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:44,837
You, me, and…

351
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,338
- and, and… Janine!
- You want me

352
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:47,381
to turn my back on my family?!

353
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:51,093
Leave Dad?

354
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:53,220
Is that what you want me to do?!

355
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:56,807
I wish it were that simple.

356
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:59,143
That would be better.

357
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:03,564
But what if your father is

358
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,025
evil?

359
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,197
That if he were gone from this world,

360
00:17:13,657 --> 00:17:17,161
the world's problems
would somehow be diminished?

361
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:21,582
Your anger toward your father
runs deep, huh.

362
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:24,251
But I understand you.

363
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:26,545
Because

364
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:31,425
the people who should
guide us to what's right

365
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:35,054
are the ones living in the wrong.

366
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:39,224
We lose our life compass.

367
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,480
So, we end up lost.

368
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:48,692
I already did that.

369
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:52,780
I already said everything
I needed to say to my dad.

370
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:56,742
I don't need to go back there.

371
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:00,329
Maybe

372
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:03,165
I'll grow old here instead.

373
00:18:05,834 --> 00:18:07,795
You already did that before, didn't you?

374
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:12,257
When you were on the island?

375
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:14,343
You turned your back on them too, right?

376
00:18:14,426 --> 00:18:17,304
Come on, Audrey! Let's leave with Janine.

377
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:21,266
Dad has changed.

378
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,437
Do you know he won't
press charges against you

379
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:27,564
because he's thinking of me and Janine?

380
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:30,818
[pensive music playing]

381
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:31,860
We are the family.

382
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:35,531
You, me, Janine. We're family!

383
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:36,990
That's what matters most!

384
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,450
- We--
- We're the family!

385
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:43,122
But how can I tell our child
that you almost killed her grandfather?!

386
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:47,751
[in English] Tell me! Tell me!

387
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:51,672
Will we be safe with you?!

388
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:54,258
Especially with your line of work!

389
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:58,720
I don't know where
we're headed anymore, Atoy.

390
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:09,064
[Audrey sobs]

391
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,566
I'm taking my child.

392
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,734
[melancholic music playing]

393
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:14,027
[in English] Please.

394
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:16,613
- Let's talk about this, please.
- [sobs]

395
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:21,535
[Audrey] Janine, child?

396
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:26,540
Did Dad hurt Grandpa?

397
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:29,918
- [Janine] Huh?
- [Audrey] Child.

398
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:34,423
- [Audrey] Let's go, my child.
- [Atoy] Child, no.

399
00:19:35,007 --> 00:19:36,216
- [Audrey, in English] Please.
- Janine.

400
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:41,847
[dramatic music playing]

401
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:56,445
[knock on door]

402
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:58,030
[door clicks open]

403
00:19:58,113 --> 00:20:00,324
[Gavin, in English] Mom, what happened?

404
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:02,034
[pensive music playing]

405
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:02,951
That's it.

406
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:04,828
[Martina sighs]

407
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,789
[Martina, in English] This is Atoy.

408
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:10,792
He beat up your dad
and shot your grandfather.

409
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,921
[in English] What? Why would he do that?

410
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:15,881
[in English] He claims that your dad

411
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:18,967
was the one
who ran over his father, which is a lie!

412
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:21,011
He doesn't even have evidence.

413
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:23,388
[in English] He tried to kill your dad.

414
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:25,641
Thankfully, your grandfather stopped him.

415
00:20:25,724 --> 00:20:28,268
[sighs] That man is truly evil.

416
00:20:29,853 --> 00:20:30,812
[knock on door]

417
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:32,314
[door clicks open]

418
00:20:32,397 --> 00:20:33,732
Excuse me, ma'am.

419
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,275
You're needed
at the nurse's station for a moment.

420
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:37,402
[in English] Okay. Stay
with your dad, okay?

421
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:38,779
[in English] I'll-- I'll be back.

422
00:20:38,862 --> 00:20:40,155
[sighs]

423
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:45,202
[suspicious music playing]

424
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:49,957
[in English] Gavin, that Atoy guy…

425
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,668
He's Karla's brother, right?

426
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:56,380
[in English] I-- I can't believe
he would do something like this.

427
00:20:56,463 --> 00:20:59,508
[music fades]

428
00:20:59,591 --> 00:21:01,260
[Atoy] <i>You have other friends, don't you?</i>

429
00:21:02,177 --> 00:21:04,137
I want you to stay away from Karla.

430
00:21:04,221 --> 00:21:07,766
Brother Atoy, I don't have
bad intentions toward Karla.

431
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:08,809
I know.

432
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:12,813
I don't need to explain myself to you.

433
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:14,856
Believe me.

434
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,651
This is better for her.

435
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:24,241
And also, do you know where
your father will be tomorrow?

436
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:29,204
I just need to ask him something.

437
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:33,875
[in English] He asked me
where my dad was last night.

438
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:35,919
Turns out he already had--

439
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:37,796
had something bad planned for Dad.

440
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:47,514
[music fades]

441
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:50,684
Atoy.

442
00:21:53,937 --> 00:21:55,272
Are you okay?

443
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:04,406
I just really wanted
to have a happy, complete family.

444
00:22:05,615 --> 00:22:08,493
[melancholic music playing]

445
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:12,497
I thought it would happen
when Audrey and Janine were given to me.

446
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:19,296
But it seems like it was just a drawing.

447
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:25,010
Like a drawing slowly being erased.

448
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:32,601
We're still here, Tatoy.

449
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:39,274
We may not be blood-related, but…

450
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:41,818
we're still your family.

451
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:47,199
We're not a drawing that can be erased.

452
00:22:48,950 --> 00:22:54,998
[melodramatic music playing]

453
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,253
Brother, I'm here.

454
00:23:00,879 --> 00:23:01,963
Me and Mama.

455
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:05,884
How are you?

456
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:08,261
I haven't seen you in a long time.

457
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:10,430
I missed you.

458
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,100
Oh?

459
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:17,729
It's really just you and Godmother Cita

460
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:21,483
who've always been there for me.

461
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:23,902
Ever since,

462
00:23:24,945 --> 00:23:28,323
you've been consistent, since day one.

463
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:31,576
[melancholic music playing]

464
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:34,204
Brother, sorry if
I haven't been around lately.

465
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:37,415
Sorry if I've been stubborn.

466
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:53,390
[sentimental music playing]

467
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:20,292
[music fades]

468
00:24:20,375 --> 00:24:26,548
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

469
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:31,887
What's the news?

470
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:34,472
[Roger] <i>I found the nun</i>
<i>Boss Red was looking for.</i>

471
00:24:34,556 --> 00:24:35,682
<i>She's with her niece.</i>

472
00:24:35,765 --> 00:24:38,351
Don't take your eyes off them.

473
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:41,354
- Who is this?
- I'm Sister Norma's niece.

474
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:42,814
[Faye] We're here in Manila now.

475
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:46,776
She wants to talk to you
about Ibyang's parents.

476
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,612
Gavin told me something.

477
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,530
I've known you since you were a child.

478
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,199
I know when you're lying.

479
00:24:52,991 --> 00:24:54,826
Are you hiding something from me?

480
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:57,287
So, does this mean

481
00:24:57,871 --> 00:25:00,582
I'll finally meet my real parents?

482
00:25:00,665 --> 00:25:01,833
Oh? Aren't you happy?

483
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:04,502
I'm just thinking of Master Grumpy.

484
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:08,215
If that happens, I might leave him.

485
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:09,841
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

486
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:13,803
UP NEXT

487
00:25:14,763 --> 00:25:16,681
[Emerson] Hey, 'Toy.

488
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:22,062
Don't touch… Miss Cita's bag.

489
00:25:22,145 --> 00:25:24,272
Go up to your room.

490
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:28,693
[music swells]

491
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:31,238
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

492
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:32,197
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
